    "details": "The Curl project reports:\n\n> - local interface connection reuse mixup (CVE-2026-107929)\n> - info leak uploading over WebSockets with GnuTLS (CVE-2026-107928)\n> - password leak in CURLINFO_EFFECTIVE_URL (CVE-2026-94266)\n> - Authorization: Negotiate sent to foreign origin (CVE-2026-94265)\n> - server-set cookie aborts cookie jar load (CVE-2026-92386)\n> - never-ending loop via server response omission (CVE-2026-92387)\n> - FTP wildcard write callback mixup (CVE-2026-92388)\n> - TFTP direction confusion (CVE-2026-92389)\n> - -J no-clobber guarantee bypassed with 103 early hints\n>   (CVE-2026-92390)\n> - curl_mime_free stack overflow by recursion (CVE-2026-92391)\n> - HTTP/2 upload Use-After-Free (CVE-2026-92392)\n> - redirect to SFTP or SCP bypasses host verification (CVE-2026-86410)\n> - server-set cookie erases cookie jar (CVE-2026-86412)\n> - Negotiate credentials sent to redirected origin (CVE-2026-86413)\n> - leaking host credentials to HTTP proxy (CVE-2026-86414)\n> - auto client cert connection reuse mixup (CVE-2026-86415)\n> - cross-origin reuse of a Negotiate connection (CVE-2026-87861)\n> - HSTS cache import drops longer-lived child (CVE-2026-87862)\n> - HSTS response erases persisted entries (CVE-2026-87863)\n> - knownhost callback mismatches key as missing (CVE-2026-87865)\n> - wolfSSL public-key pinning bypass (CVE-2026-87866)\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0512",
